                                                "sense_id": "adcbf2ca-f5f6-316c-88c6-94c2c52d4f6f",
                                                "text": "Many of the most earnest Protestants were business men, to whom lending money at interest was essential. Consequently first Calvin, and then other Protestant divines, sanctioned interest."
                                            }
                                        ]
